# HPC (DTU)

**Do not run heavy work on the login node** (`hpclogin*`). Login is for editing, git, and `bsub` submission only.

| Task | Where |
|------|--------|
| Train / validate / **pytest** / data loading at scale | **Compute node** |
| Interactive shell on compute | `linuxsh` then `cd /work3/s204070/SPA` and `source .venv/bin/activate` |
| Batch jobs | `bsub < hpc/submit/...` (scripts must `cd` to repo root) |

**Prefer `bsub` over long interactive runs** when a submit script exists (`hpc/submit/decoder_only/`, etc.).

**Never run `pytest` on the login node** — not even a single test file. Use `bsub < hpc/submit/tests/run_pytest.sh` or an interactive compute shell (`linuxsh`, then activate venv and run pytest there).

**Do not** start full training, multi-epoch smoke, or validation on the login node either.

After code changes that affect training, point the user to the matching submit script rather than re-running old checkpoints.
